    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "description",
      "value": "Implement gradient flow rigidity hypothesis test: construct 5 distinct analytic constraint functions (polynomial, trigonometric, piecewise smooth) generating w ∈ {10, 20, 50, 100} sample points in [0,1]. Train single-hidden-layer tanh networks with widths N ∈ {1,2,...,50} using gradient descent (10k steps, learning rate decay). Record maximum absolute error on held-out constraint points. Determine N_c(w) as minimal width achieving error ≤ 1e-3 for each w. Repeat 5 times per (w,N) with random seeds; verify N_c(w) stability. Compare trend against prediction that N_c(w) remains bounded (≤20) as w increases."
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "skill",
      "value": "neural_network_capacity_scan"
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "expected_prediction",
      "value": "N_c(w) values will be finite and bounded (e.g., N_c(10)=5, N_c(20)=7, N_c(50)=9, N_c(100)=11), showing no significant growth with w; all seeds will yield N_c(w) ≤ 20 with standard deviation < 2. Training and held-out errors at N_c(w) will be ≤ 8e-4."
    },
    {
